{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-dec4d976-8ffb-475a-8e97-d82eea1d4c52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a44f105049ee832e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-hiqgx185/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E003.md","content":"# Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set PostgreSQL resource sizing\n\n## Description\n\nSprint-1 benchmark that captures the inline Milvus provider baseline and verifies that pgvector performs in the same order of magnitude for typical Gen AI Studio playground RAG usage, plus a recommended resource sizing for the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance. The default store is positioned for development experimentation, not production usage: strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99) are not required, and typical playground RAG usage involves small document sets where a flat scan (no index) is sufficient. The benchmark runs against a self-provisioned dev/test pgvector instance and does not depend on the production provisioning mechanism selected for the platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Stand up a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance in a development/test environment using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector is included out of the box — no custom image build is needed).\n- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline for representative playground RAG workloads (small document sets, insertion and retrieval).\n- Run the same workloads against pgvector with flat scan (no index) and compare results.\n- Produce a benchmark report stating the order-of-magnitude comparison — not a pass/fail against specific latency thresholds — and confirming flat-scan suitability for typical playground usage.\n- Derive recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits for the default instance, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits as the reference values, adjusted based on the benchmark findings.\n- Position the default store in the report: development experimentation scope, with users holding production-scale vector workloads directed to an external vector database.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A benchmark report exists that documents the inline Milvus baseline measurements, the pgvector measurements, and an order-of-magnitude comparison for representative playground RAG workloads.\n- The report confirms (or flags) that flat scan over small document sets is sufficient for the default store's intended usage.\n- Recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are documented, explicitly referencing the model-registry-operator values as the starting point and the benchmark-driven adjustments.\n- The report states the positioning of the default store (development experimentation; production-scale workloads should use an external vector database).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — the order-of-magnitude comparison against the inline Milvus baseline is the measurable form of \"no loss\" for dev-experimentation scope.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" — the sizing recommendation derived here.\n- Staff Engineer Input: sprint-1 benchmark scope (baseline capture, order of magnitude, no thresholds, flat scan) and PostgreSQL resource sizing direction (model-registry-operator reference values, adjusted per benchmarking).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91500,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85a45358e228944","agent_id":"a2b696fdb420d40ad","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"ef761e9c-149f-4471-8c6a-5db77f0c44cb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T1