{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9da39be1-42fe-4b5b-bc46-ce8420e2ee55","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bde945ca6c893354","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-hiqgx185/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch A of the provisioning decision: implemented when the go/no-go gate confirms that the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5. This epic implements PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management for the Gen AI Studio default vector store in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern, and carries the end-to-end validation of the out-of-box RAG experience for this approach. The existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) is used — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding is needed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning and lifecycle management (creation, deletion, credential management, persistent storage) in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization. The upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n- Follow the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern: a per-scope PostgreSQL Deployment, Service, credentials Secret, and persistent storage, using the `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` image (pgvector included out of the box).\n- Support disconnected installs via the related-image environment variable for the PostgreSQL image, which is already present in the rhods-operator CSV.\n- Scope the provisioned instance per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace is the preferred default for multi-tenant isolation).\n- Set PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's reference values, adjusted per the sprint-1 benchmark findings when available.\n- End-to-end validation of the out-of-box experience: a playground with RAG configured gets a working default vector store with zero manual steps, and RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability with the remote pgvector provider enabled.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Gen AI Studio playground configured with RAG capabilities gets a working default pgvector vector store with zero manual provisioning or configuration steps by the user.\n- The PostgreSQL instance lifecycle (creation, deletion, credential management) is fully managed by the operator, scoped per the confirmed model with per-namespace isolation between tenants.\n- The provisioned PostgreSQL runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server instance (not an inline provider).\n- PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator reference values and documented, with benchmark-driven adjustments noted.\n- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function end-to-end with the remote pgvector vector_io provider enabled, with no loss of current capability.\n- The provisioned instance's connection details are consumed by the playground's pgvector vector_io configuration via a Kubernetes secret.\n- On a simulated disconnected install, the PostgreSQL image is resolved through the related-image environment variable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" — this epic is the operator-based delivery of that capability under branch outcome A.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — end-to-end validation included in this epic's scope.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\".\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\".\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" — resource requests/limits applied to the provisioned instance (bundled: the sizing is applied on the same provisioning surface this epic owns; splitting it would require a second pass over the same deployment templates).\n- Staff Engineer Input: operator dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164, model-registry-operator pattern, existing pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL image, related-image env var already in the rhods-operator CSV, resource sizing reference.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92273,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85a45358e228944","agent_id":"a2b696fdb420d40ad","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"9b0d0ce1-87eb-48fa-a08c-745d4de7e55e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:29:43.381Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
