results in working Gen AI Studio playground RAG via the pgvector vector_io provider, with no manual steps beyond the documented configuration.\n- When neither a default vector store nor a user connection is available, the playground presents a clear, actionable error describing the required configuration.\n- The user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own PostgreSQL setup is delivered and technically reviewed against the implementation.\n- Playground RAG against the user-supplied database runs with the vector store as a separate process from the OGX server instance (not an inline provider).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — under branch outcome C the capability is preserved through customer-supplied PostgreSQL; this is the explicit degraded-mode exception to the out-of-the-box criterion, per the fallback direction in the Staff Engineer Input.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\".\n- Staff Engineer Input: fallback requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer CR spec configuration; alignment with OGX 1.0 breaking changes; PostgreSQL is a supported OGX backend when user-configured with an explicit connection-string secret.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":94470,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85a45358e228944","agent_id":"a2b696fdb420d40ad","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"ae974d2c-a720-4f5a-900e-ffa1b42ac139","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:30:08.181Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
