{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad992cdcaa5c1abc","type":"tool_result","content":"125:10. `konflux-onboarding` ∥ general implementation parallel (config independent of code; AC gates first execution). **Add NO blocking edge in either direction.** It is tempting to make the general implementation depend on `konflux-onboarding` (\"the code needs a build pipeline first\") — do not. That coupling is enforced by the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC on the general implementation epic, never by a DAG dependency. A `konflux-onboarding → general` edge serializes work that must run in parallel and is a rule violation. This holds for EVERY `konflux-onboarding` × general-implementation pair in the decomposition, whatever the general epic's component or deliverable — a stack-wide assembly, packaging, or evidence epic that consumes the pipeline's outputs is still a general implementation. There is no \"different component\" or \"genuine artifact dependency\" exemption: if the coupling is real, express it as an AC on the consuming epic (\"the signed attestations from the build pipeline are included and validated\"), never as an edge.\n146:23. Strategy replaces existing capability → add rollback/feature-flag AC to replacing Implementation epic\n248:- Implementation-specific requirements (build pipeline green, rollback plan, doc review, etc.)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8f8f198478e2793","agent_id":"a9f3dec29b468d8b4","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"bd06f974-0a15-4048-960e-76dfce9e656f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:34:41.529Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad992cdcaa5c1abc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
