rides. Two rule violations force criterion zeros: a work-product type mixing in BRANCH-C-E004 (code bundled with content authoring) and a missing rule-mandated rollback/feature-flag AC on the replacing epic E002. Both are localized fixes; the rest of the plan does not need rework.\n34\t\n35\t## Criterion Details\n36\t\n37\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n38\t\n39\tThe strategy has no HLR section (full strategy is in an unavailable attachment — logged in Health Warnings); the traceability matrix maps the strategy's Acceptance Criteria plus Staff Engineer Input directives instead, which is the right adaptation. Every AC is accounted for: AC-1/2/4/5/6 map to specific epics; AC-3 (Auto Rag) is explicitly removed with justification (SEI-6, deferred to RHAISTRAT-7824) — logged as an override, not silently dropped. Priority inheritance holds: E001 (P0) gates the P0 branch epics; E003 is P1 and blocks no P0 work, with the rationale recorded in Health Warnings. Bundling decisions (E001's scoping-model decision; sizing within the branch provisioning epics) are recorded in the matrix rows with inline `(bundled)` rationale and share the same implementation/decision surface as the P0 work — compliant with the bundling exception. Sizing (AC-6) coverage does not hinge on the P1 benchmark: the branch epics apply model-registry-operator reference values with benchmark adjustment as an AC.\n40\t\n41\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n42\t\n43\tNo circular dependencies; all edges reference existing epics. Frontmatter `dependencies` match the diagram edge-for-edge (E001→BRANCH-A/B/C-E004; E002→E003), and the diagram uses the correct dependency→dependent convention. Branch files all set both `branch` (matching filename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`, with `gated_by` present in each branch epic's direct `dependencies`. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in `dependencies`. All three gate edges have `gate_failure_impact` with `action: remove` and a concrete `fallback_approach`. The E002→E003