\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n52\t\n53\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome determines which of three downstream branch epics exists (the definition of a structural gate), and it resolves the scoping-model open question. Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (BFF wiring + tests, benchmark report, provisioning controllers/resources, configuration support). Every `gated_by` is set only where a true gate exists, each with both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated. Every `gated_by` target (E001) appears in the epic's direct `dependencies`. E003's dependency on E002 is an Implementation→Implementation edge needing no gate. No misclassifications.\n54\t\n55\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n56\t\n57\tType-appropriate signal sets are used throughout (E001 carries `investigation_signals`; all Implementation epics carry `ai_signals`; no cross-assignment). E001's signals are well-calibrated: `source_accessibility: 0` and `human_judgment_required: -2` correctly reflect that the gating answer (RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery timing) does not exist in any readable artifact and is a sprint-planning decision. E002's `open_questions: 0` honestly acknowledges the connection-secret ownership variance rather than claiming full resolution. `architecture_claims: 1` rationales are corroborated against the actual context files: ogx-distribution.md confirms PGVector as a remote vector I/O backend via env-guarded providers; model-registry-operator.md confirms the auto-provisioned `{registry-name}-postgres` pattern; odh-dashboard.md confirms the gen-ai BFF sidecar with Kubernetes resource creation and guardrails integration; ogx-k8s-operator.md supports the RHOAI-operator-layer premise. No calibration misses. No arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n58\t\n59\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (0/2)\n60\t\n61\tACs are present, specific, and testable across all six epics. No non-testable/externally-controlled precondition ACs — the RHAISTRAT-7164 schedule risk is correctly filed in Health Warnings, not as an AC. No draft-ID (E00x) references in epic bodies. Branch C's documentation AC includes technical review against the implementation.\n62\t\n63\tHowever, **E002 is the replacing Implementation epic and lacks the rule-mandated rollback/feature-flag AC**. The strategy replaces the playground's existing vector-store backing (inline Milvus embedded in the OGX distribution) with the remote pgvector provider, and E002 is the epic that flips that default on every BFF-created OGXServer instance. Per the AC rules (replacement → rollback/feature-flag AC on the replacing epic), E002 needs an AC establishing that the provider enablement is revertible/toggleable by configuration (e.g., falling back to the prior provider configuration without a code change). None of E002's five ACs covers rollback or a feature flag. Missing rule-mandated AC → major issue → criterion scores 0.\n64\t\n65\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n66\t\n67\tAll strategy scope is covered: out-of-box default store (branch epics), provider wiring (E002), separate-process requirement (E002 + branches), multi-tenant scoping (E001 decision + branch implementation), lightweight sizing (E003 + branch ACs), no-loss validation (E002 integration tests, E003 order-of-magnitude comparison, branch E2E ACs). The Auto Rag removal is a Staff-Engineer-directed scope change, logged as an override with the receiving strategy (RHAISTRAT-7824) named. Strategy-level context is carried, not dropped: the RHAISTRAT-7164 timing risk and the unresolved migration-path open question are both in Health Warnings with their disposition; the go/no-go gate directive from the Staff Engineer Input is E001's core deliverable. Conditional branches cover all three bounded outcomes named in the Staff Engineer Input (operator-based, BFF-managed, customer-supplied). No docs-authoring epic is required: the strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section (attachment missing), so no `Documentation Support: Yes` exists to trigger Rule 11 (validator confirms).\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3e7679c48fa5da5","agent_id":"a84b1f058f9da17e6","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"537233ec-a97d-47c1-b68d-25e0bd3f9d84","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:37:13.534Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a884faab2f5822da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
