{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-881fe5454942e617","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E004\n3\ttitle: Customer-supplied PostgreSQL configuration support for Gen AI Studio RAG (branch\n4\t  C)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: C\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If a self-provisioning approach (operator-based or BFF-managed)\n17\t    is selected at the go/no-go gate, this epic is not implemented; its user-documentation\n18\t    scope may be retained as guidance for users who prefer their own database.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Customer-supplied PostgreSQL configuration support for Gen AI Studio RAG (branch C)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional branch C of the provisioning decision: the degraded-mode fallback, implemented when the go/no-go gate determines that neither self-provisioning approach (operator-based or BFF-managed) is viable for RHOAI 3.5. Customers bring their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the playground, configuring the OGXServer custom resource spec with their PostgreSQL connection details. This aligns with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0, even though the playground largely abstracts OGX from users. The epic delivers the configuration support, validation and error handling in the gen-ai BFF, user-facing documentation of the setup, and end-to-end validation of playground RAG against a user-supplied database.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Support user-configured PostgreSQL connection details (a connection-string secret) on the OGXServer custom resource spec, consumed by the remote pgvector vector_io provider for playground RAG.\n44\t- Implement BFF validation and clear, actionable error handling and messaging in the playground when no default vector store is available and no user connection is configured.\n45\t- Author user-facing documentation of the required OGXServer spec configuration for bringing your own PostgreSQL (the substantive content deliverable of this branch).\n46\t- End-to-end validation: playground RAG workflows function against a user-supplied PostgreSQL instance with the remote pgvector provider enabled.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A user-configured PostgreSQL connection on the OGXServer spec results in working Gen AI Studio playground RAG via the pgvector vector_io provider, with no manual steps beyond the documented configuration.\n51\t- When neither a default vector store nor a user connection is available, the playground presents a clear, actionable error describing the required configuration.\n52\t- The user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own PostgreSQL setup is delivered and technically reviewed against the implementation.\n53\t- Playground RAG against the user-supplied database runs with the vector store as a separate process from the OGX server instance (not an inline provider).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — under branch outcome C the capability is preserved through customer-supplied PostgreSQL; this is the explicit degraded-mode exception to the out-of-the-box criterion, per the fallback direction in the Staff Engineer Input.\n58\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\".\n59\t- Staff Engineer Input: fallback requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer CR spec configuration; alignment with OGX 1.0 breaking changes; PostgreSQL is a supported OGX backend when user-configured with an explicit connection-string secret.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3e7679c48fa5da5","agent_id":"a84b1f058f9da17e6","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"357c80ee-5505-436f-aa12-878f9528e4b6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:37:20.775Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-881fe5454942e617","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
