{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-894f518f132fc701","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\t  OGXServer instances\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tWire the odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF to configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider on the OGXServer instances it creates for the playground, so that playground RAG capabilities no longer depend on the inline Milvus provider embedded in the OGX distribution image. The existing remote vector store implementation is largely reused — the integration effort is configuration wiring, not new provider code. This work is required under every provisioning outcome (operator-based, BFF-managed, or customer-supplied PostgreSQL) and proceeds independently of that decision.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation (the code path that currently hardcodes the SQLite storage settings, e.g. `llamastack_config.go`) to enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider (e.g. the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` configuration) with connection settings referencing the PostgreSQL instance's credentials.\n39\t- Consume the PostgreSQL connection details from whichever source is in effect — a platform-provisioned default instance or a user-supplied connection — via a Kubernetes secret, without hardcoding credentials.\n40\t- Keep the vector storage configuration strictly independent of the OGX application storage backend: the application storage backend remains on its existing default (SQLite). No SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is performed and no consolidation of vector and application storage is introduced.\n41\t- Reuse the existing remote vector store implementation in the OGX distribution; no changes to the OGX distribution image or its provider code are in scope.\n42\t- Unit and integration tests covering provider activation, connection wiring, and the independence of vector storage from application storage configuration.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- A playground created with RAG capabilities gets an OGXServer instance whose vector_io provider is the remote pgvector provider, with the vector store running as a separate process from the OGX server (not an inline provider).\n47\t- The OGX application storage backend configuration is unchanged from its existing default; no migration of application storage occurs.\n48\t- PostgreSQL credentials are consumed from a Kubernetes secret; no credentials are hardcoded in the BFF or the OGXServer spec.\n49\t- Existing Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows operate against pgvector with no loss of current capability in a development/test environment.\n50\t- Integration tests demonstrate that enabling the pgvector vector_io provider does not alter the application storage backend settings.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" — this epic delivers the provider side of that capability.\n55\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — provider wiring is the enabling change.\n56\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\" — the remote provider configuration is exactly this decoupling.\n57\t- Staff Engineer Input: the existing remote vector store implementation is reusable; vector storage and application storage are independent configurations; the ogx-distribution already ships the remote pgvector vector I/O backend.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3e7679c48fa5da5","agent_id":"a84b1f058f9da17e6","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"6bdd5ccf-18d3-4644-aa04-d281aa3cea4f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:37:21.311Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-894f518f132fc701","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
