iguration with a user-supplied connection-string secret. The documentation is written and technically reviewed against the implemented configuration support, the remote pgvector provider wiring, and the confirmed resource-sizing guidance, so it runs last within branch C.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Author user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL setup for Gen AI Studio playground RAG: the OGXServer custom resource spec fields for PostgreSQL connection details, creation of the connection-string secret, and any prerequisites a user must complete.\n- Document the degraded-mode behavior users see when neither a default vector store nor a user connection is configured, and the steps to resolve it (matching the actionable error messaging delivered by the configuration support).\n- Include resource-sizing guidance for user-supplied PostgreSQL instances, starting from the model-registry-operator reference values and reflecting the benchmark findings.\n- Technically review the documentation against the implemented behavior and correct any divergence found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL setup is delivered and covers the complete configuration procedure: OGXServer spec connection details, connection-string secret creation, and verification of working playground RAG.\n- A user following the documented procedure on a clean cluster gets working Gen AI Studio playground RAG against their own PostgreSQL instance via the remote pgvector vector_io provider, with no manual steps beyond the documented configuration.\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation and updated for any divergence found during review.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" — under branch outcome C this is the explicit degraded-mode exception: the documented bring-your-own procedure is how users reach the capability, per the fallback direction in the Staff Engineer Input.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — under branch outcome C, users reach working playground RAG by following this documentation.\n- Staff Engineer Input: fallback requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer CR spec configuration; alignment with OGX 1.0 breaking changes; PostgreSQL is a supported OGX backend when user-configured with an explicit connection-string secret.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35517,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3e7679c48fa5da5","agent_id":"a84b1f058f9da17e6","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"9d48877f-cb54-4906-8f46-70a3d8a4ced8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:39:12.991Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
