{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74f6496fb48335e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch\n4\t  A)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5, this epic\n18\t    does not exist; the selected fallback is BFF-managed provisioning or customer-supplied\n19\t    PostgreSQL per the go/no-go decision.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 5\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional branch A of the provisioning decision: implemented when the go/no-go gate confirms that the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for RHOAI 3.5. This epic implements PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management for the Gen AI Studio default vector store in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern, and carries the end-to-end validation of the out-of-box RAG experience for this approach. The existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) is used — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding is needed.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning and lifecycle management (creation, deletion, credential management, persistent storage) in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization. The upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n45\t- Follow the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern: a per-scope PostgreSQL Deployment, Service, credentials Secret, and persistent storage, using the `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` image (pgvector included out of the box).\n46\t- Support disconnected installs via the related-image environment variable for the PostgreSQL image, which is already present in the rhods-operator CSV.\n47\t- Scope the provisioned instance per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace is the preferred default for multi-tenant isolation).\n48\t- Set PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's reference values, adjusted per the sprint-1 benchmark findings when available.\n49\t- End-to-end validation of the out-of-box experience: a playground with RAG configured gets a working default vector store with zero manual steps, and RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability with the remote pgvector provider enabled.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A Gen AI Studio playground configured with RAG capabilities gets a working default pgvector vector store with zero manual provisioning or configuration steps by the user.\n54\t- The PostgreSQL instance lifecycle (creation, deletion, credential management) is fully managed by the operator, scoped per the confirmed model with per-namespace isolation between tenants.\n55\t- The provisioned PostgreSQL runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server instance (not an inline provider).\n56\t- PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator reference values and documented, with benchmark-driven adjustments noted.\n57\t- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function end-to-end with the remote pgvector vector_io provider enabled, with no loss of current capability.\n58\t- The provisioned instance's connection details are consumed by the playground's pgvector vector_io configuration via a Kubernetes secret.\n59\t- On a simulated disconnected install, the PostgreSQL image is resolved through the related-image environment variable.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" — this epic is the operator-based delivery of that capability under branch outcome A.\n64\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — end-to-end validation included in this epic's scope.\n65\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider)\".\n66\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation)\".\n67\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead\" — resource requests/limits applied to the provisioned instance (bundled: the sizing is applied on the same provisioning surface this epic owns; splitting it would require a second pass over the same deployment templates).\n68\t- Staff Engineer Input: operator dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164, model-registry-operator pattern, existing pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL image, related-image env var already in the rhods-operator CSV, resource sizing reference.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-988303e1dab42617","agent_id":"ab2a1f821930acc44","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"543e3c3a-671c-4172-9015-0961db0b8796","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:40:39.044Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74f6496fb48335e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
