 technically reviewed against the implemented configuration support, the remote pgvector provider wiring, and the confirmed resource-sizing guidance, so it runs last within branch C.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Author user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL setup for Gen AI Studio playground RAG: the OGXServer custom resource spec fields for PostgreSQL connection details, creation of the connection-string secret, and any prerequisites a user must complete.\n47\t- Document the degraded-mode behavior users see when neither a default vector store nor a user connection is configured, and the steps to resolve it (matching the actionable error messaging delivered by the configuration support).\n48\t- Include resource-sizing guidance for user-supplied PostgreSQL instances, starting from the model-registry-operator reference values and reflecting the benchmark findings.\n49\t- Technically review the documentation against the implemented behavior and correct any divergence found.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The user-facing documentation of the bring-your-own-PostgreSQL setup is delivered and covers the complete configuration procedure: OGXServer spec connection details, connection-string secret creation, and verification of working playground RAG.\n54\t- A user following the documented procedure on a clean cluster gets working Gen AI Studio playground RAG against their own PostgreSQL instance via the remote pgvector vector_io provider, with no manual steps beyond the documented configuration.\n55\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation and updated for any divergence found during review.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\" — under branch outcome C this is the explicit degraded-mode exception: the documented bring-your-own procedure is how users reach the capability, per the fallback direction in the Staff Engineer Input.\n60\t- Strategy acceptance criterion \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\" — under branch outcome C, users reach working playground RAG by following this documentation.\n61\t- Staff Engineer Input: fallback requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer CR spec configuration; alignment with OGX 1.0 breaking changes; PostgreSQL is a supported OGX backend when user-configured with an explicit connection-string secret.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-988303e1dab42617","agent_id":"ab2a1f821930acc44","session_id":"c797c45b-eabe-4faf-a684-66c1833f1941","uuid":"ca3a6f4f-2e0b-4fe1-9042-98e0e14fb586","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:40:41.050Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab2b54fa84c3a381","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
